Rational Owned Choice: Player Views, Sharp Tests, and Intrinsic Fragments

The paper is main.tex. Select it as the main document in Overleaf and use
pdfLaTeX, or build locally with TeX Live and latexmk:

    make paper

The PDF is build/main.pdf. To create an upload containing only the paper
sources and bibliography:

    make overleaf

Upload build/overleaf.zip to Overleaf. The mathematical statements,
proofs, attribution, and proof-status inventory are all in the paper.

Layout:

    main.tex          Paper entry point
    references.bib    Bibliography
    sections/         Paper sections, appendices, and macros
    lean/             Eight Lean proof modules, using only Std
    checks/           Python models and independent finite checks
    lean-toolchain    Lean version (4.34.1)
    build/            Generated PDF, upload ZIP, and compiled proofs

Run all verification with Python 3 and Lean installed through elan:

    make check

make check-python and make check-lean run either part separately. Python
needs only the standard library. Lean imports are built in dependency
order, with generated files under build/lean. make clean removes build/.
checks/probe_residual.py is an optional experiment, outside the checks;
it establishes no residual bound for the whole variety.

The paper distinguishes kernel-checked results, written generic proofs,
and finite checks. The dependent data-calculus metatheory and general
hidden-game composition are not certified by the algebraic Lean modules.

Earlier drafts and tracked reviews are available in Git history through
69f763a. Uncommitted reviews are retained locally in .git/local-notes/.
